            <ArticleTitle>Dorsal column stimulation: optimization of application.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>142-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Results are reviewed of dorsal column electrical stimulation for chronic pain in a series of 80 patients. In the light of the experience gained from this series, indications and patient suitability for this form of therapy are discussed. Complications occurring after implantation are tabulated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
